{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T09:21:50.209Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_097e671233ad69b5016a608babecdc8190be0706ab77d171e1","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The translated module now parses and executes under the new semantics: `krun solution.mpy` installs exactly the emitted function body. The runtime semantics covers statement sequencing, returns, call environments, integer/string evaluation, branching, `len`, and the two slice forms actually used by the solution; next I’m wiring the universal recursive claim to an independent overlap-count recurrence."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f891c-793d-7953-86ac-83de05208d84"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T09:22:01.396Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_097e671233ad69b5016a608bae2a20819080e1fc44c0f94e14","status":"completed","call_id":"call_uSmcaFFc3JFvq7Zpg5lXQGyk","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /work/run-example.mpy\\n+Module(\\n+  FuncDef(\\\"how_many_times\\\", Params(\\\"string\\\", \\\"substring\\\"),\\n+    If(Compare(Name(\\\"substring\\\"), CmpOp(\\\"==\\\", Str(\\\"\\\"))),\\n+      Return(BinOp(\\\"+\\\", Call(Name(\\\"len\\\"), Name(\\\"string\\\")), Int(1))),\\n+      )\\n+    If(Compare(\\n+      Call(Name(\\\"len\\\"), Name(\\\"string\\\")),\\n+      CmpOp(\\\"<\\\", Call(Name(\\\"len\\\"), Name(\\\"substring\\\")))),\\n+      Return(Int(0)),\\n+      )\\n+    If(Compare(\\n+      Subscript(\\n+        Name(\\\"string\\\"),\\n+        Slice(NoBound, Call(Name(\\\"len\\\"), Name(\\\"substring\\\")), NoBound)),\\n+      CmpOp(\\\"==\\\", Name(\\\"substring\\\"))),\\n+      Return(\\n+        BinOp(\\n+          \\\"+\\\",\\n+          Int(1),\\n+          Call(\\n+            Name(\\\"how_many_times\\\"),\\n+            Subscript(Name(\\\"string\\\"), Slice(Int(1), NoBound, NoBound)),\\n+            Name(\\\"substring\\\")))),\\n+      )\\n+    Return(\\n+      Call(\\n+        Name(\\\"how_many_times\\\"),\\n+        Subscript(Name(\\\"string\\\"), Slice(Int(1), NoBound, NoBound)),\\n+        Name(\\\"substring\\\"))))\\n+  Expr(Call(Name(\\\"how_many_times\\\"), Str(\\\"aaaa\\\"), Str(\\\"aa\\\"))))\\n*** Add File: /work/spec.k\\n+requires \\\"verification.k\\\"\\n+\\n+module SPEC\\n+  imports VERIFICATION\\n+\\n+  // Universal functional-correctness claim.  CONT makes the claim usable as\\n+  // the circularity at each recursive call, while ENV checks call restoration.\\n+  claim [how-many-times-correct]:\\n+    <k> invoke(strVal(S), strVal(T)) ~> CONT:K\\n+      => intVal(overlapCount(S, T)) ~> CONT </k>\\n+    <functions>\\n+      \\\"how_many_times\\\" |->\\n+        function(Params(\\\"string\\\", \\\"substring\\\"),\\n+          If(Compare(Name(\\\"substring\\\"), CmpOp(\\\"==\\\", Str(\\\"\\\"))),\\n+            Return(BinOp(\\\"+\\\", Call(Name(\\\"len\\\"), Name(\\\"string\\\")), Int(1))),\\n+            .Stmts)\\n+          If(Compare(\\n+              Call(Name(\\\"len\\\"), Name(\\\"string\\\")),\\n+              CmpOp(\\\"<\\\", Call(Name(\\\"len\\\"), Name(\\\"substring\\\")))),\\n+            Return(Int(0)),\\n+            .Stmts)\\n+          If(Compare(\\n+              Subscript(Name(\\\"string\\\"),\\n+                Slice(NoBound,\\n+                  Call(Name(\\\"len\\\"), Name(\\\"substring\\\")), NoBound)),\\n+              CmpOp(\\\"==\\\", Name(\\\"substring\\\"))),\\n+            Return(BinOp(\\\"+\\\", Int(1),\\n+              Call(Name(\\\"how_many_times\\\"),\\n+                Subscript(Name(\\\"string\\\"),\\n+                  Slice(Int(1), NoBound, NoBound)),\\n+                Name(\\\"substring\\\")))),\\n+            .Stmts)\\n+          Return(Call(Name(\\\"how_many_times\\\"),\\n+            Subscript(Name(\\\"string\\\"), Slice(Int(1), NoBound, NoBound)),\\n+            Name(\\\"substring\\\"))))\\n+    </functions>\\n+    <env> ENV:Map </env>\\n+endmodule\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"krun run-example.mpy --definition semantic-kompiled && kompile verification.k --main-module VERIFICATION --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --backend haskell\",workdir:\"/work\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:20000});\ntext(JSON.stringify(r));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f891c-793d-7953-86ac-83de05208d84"}}}
